#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports_dev.config.rst:26:<autosummary>:1
#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig:1 of
msgid "The settings of one ``freeports-dev`` invocation, already resolved."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig:3 of
msgid ""
"Built from the parsed arguments, so every subcommand reads its settings "
"the same way instead of each one inventing its own fallbacks."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.formats_repo:1 of
msgid ""
"The formats repository. Defaults to the working directory, as every "
"subcommand did."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.formats_repo:3 of
msgid ""
"The first two tiers arrive relative to the shell they were written in and"
" are resolved as such; the third is resolved against the configuration "
"file instead, which is what :func:`_from_config_dir` exists for."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.input_db_from_file:1 of
msgid ""
"The `db_path` of the configuration file, consulted only after the "
"repository's own."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.input_db_from_file:3 of
msgid ""
"Resolved against the file, for the same reason `formats_repo` is: one "
"`db_path:` line is read from every directory anybody runs a subcommand "
"in."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.input_db_override:1 of
msgid ""
"An input database named outright, or ``None`` to let the search in "
":mod:`input_db` run."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.input_db_override:3 of
msgid ""
"Deliberately not resolved to a default here: the search that follows "
"prefers a format repository's **own** ``tests/input_db`` over anything "
"the configuration file says, so that running a repository's tests does "
"not silently pick up whatever real database happens to be configured on "
"the machine. Only an explicit flag or variable overrides that."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.noconfirm:1 of
msgid "Skip the ``make-tests`` prompts."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.noconfirm:3 of
msgid ""
"An absent flag is *unset*, not false: ``--noconfirm`` can only ever turn "
"the setting on, so that a command line which does not mention it leaves "
"alone a file or environment that did."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.page_type:1 of
msgid "The page type, for the subcommands that take one."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.target_lists:1 of
msgid "The lists the tests search for."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.DevConfig.target_lists:3 of
msgid ""
"The environment variable holds **one** list, the whole raw value, never "
"split -- the same rule as the engine's ``FREEPORTS_TARGET_LIST``, so that"
" a list name containing a comma or a space means the same thing to both "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.config.set_active:3 of
msgid ""
"The pytest plugin runs in the same process as ``freeports-dev test`` but "
"is reached *through* pytest, which knows nothing of our parsed arguments."
" Rather than smuggle the answers back out through the environment -- "
"which cannot even express a list of target lists -- the command line "
"leaves the resolved object here and the plugin picks it up."
msgstr ""

